  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OECD Tax and Development 2023-27 - OECD CTPA</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">OECD Tax and Development 2023-27</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">OECD Skatt och Utveckling 2023-27
St&#xf6;det till OECDs program om skatt och utveckling inriktar sig fr&#xe4;mst mot den globala skatteproblematiken och hur den p&#xe5;verkar utvecklingsl&#xe4;nderna samt m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;r f&#xf6;r utvecklingsl&#xe4;nderna att ut&#xf6;va p&#xe5;verkan p&#xe5; de internationella regelverken f&#xf6;r att regelverken i h&#xf6;gre grad ska gynna utvecklingsl&#xe4;nderna.

OECDs Program &#xe4;r f&#xf6;rdelade enligt:
- Skatteflykt (BEPS)
- Skatteflykt (informationsutbyte)
- Skattebrott, penningtv&#xe4;tt och korruption
- Skattef&#xf6;rvaltningen
- Statistik &#xf6;ver int&#xe4;kter
- Landpolitik
- Skatteanalys
- Milj&#xf6;relaterade skatter
- Merv&#xe4;rdesskatt
- Utvecklingssamarbete, multilateral samverkan</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OECD Tax and Development 2023-27
The support to the OECD&apos;s programme on tax and development focuses primarily on the global tax problem and how it affects developing countries, and enables developing countries to exert influence on international regulations in order for the regulations to benefit developing countries to a greater extent.

OECD Programs are distributed as:
- Tax Avoidance (BEPS)
- Tax Evasion (Information Exchange)
- Tax crimes, money laundering and corruption
- Tax administration
- Revenue Statistics
- Country Policy
- Tax Analysis
- Environmentally related taxes
- Value Added Tax
- Development Co-operation</narrative>
  </description>
